  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 103.51 Sanitary survey",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 103.51 “Sanitary survey” means an on-site inspection or review of the water source(s), facilities, equipment, operation, maintenance, and monitoring of a public water system to evaluate the adequacy of the system, including its sources and operations, to ensure the distribution of safe drinking water.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Dw 100) #10606, eff 6-1-14; renumbered by #10770 (from Env-Dw 103.49); renumbered by #12180 (from Env-Dw 103.50)",
